From b888d75b8ca825c04b2168844d5d21da965d6896 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antonio Borneo <antonio.borneo@foss.st.com>
Date: Mon, 25 May 2026 16:01:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] perf: stm32: introduce DDRPERFM driver (FIX)

The access controller firewall can deny access to the ddrperfm
device, due to secure boot configuration.

Don't log an error during probe, as this is the correct behavior
for secured devices.
Dump a debug message to make it easy to track it.

Signed-off-by: Antonio Borneo <antonio.borneo@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I0130eb1b67f554cb070bea009f5c7c72012e1262
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/571215
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
---
 drivers/perf/stm32_ddr_pmu.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/perf/stm32_ddr_pmu.c b/drivers/perf/stm32_ddr_pmu.c
index 38328663d2c5..b3867fc2c1bc 100644
--- a/drivers/perf/stm32_ddr_pmu.c
+++ b/drivers/perf/stm32_ddr_pmu.c
@@ -735,6 +735,10 @@ static int stm32_ddr_pmu_device_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		if (ret)
 			return dev_err_probe(pmu->dev, ret, "Failed to get firewall\n");
 		ret = stm32_firewall_grant_access_by_id(&firewall, firewall.firewall_id);
+		if (ret == -EACCES) {
+			dev_dbg(pmu->dev, "Access denied by firewall\n");
+			return -ENODEV;
+		}
 		if (ret)
 			return dev_err_probe(pmu->dev, ret, "Failed to grant access\n");
 	}
-- 
